.TH tkurender n 0.1 tkutils
.SH tkutils::tkurender
.PP
Shared render core for the tkudesigner GUI designer and the tkuload spec loader: a widget catalogue, an in\-memory design model, \fBdeserialize\fR, and a live ttk render engine. Pure Tk/ttk; namespace \fB::tkurender\fR. This is not a widget \-\- it is the engine both frontends build on.
.SS Model
.PP
\fBnewModel\fR starts a fresh design (a single \fBroot\fR frame). Nodes are added under a parent and addressed by an opaque id.
.CS
::tkurender::newModel
set id [::tkurender::addNode type parentId ?record?]   ;# -> node id
::tkurender::deleteNode $id
.CE
.PP
The model lives in the array \fB::tkurender::D\fR (keys \fBroot\fR, \fBnodes\fR, \fBkids\fR, \fBparent\fR, \fBwpath,<id>\fR, \fBsel\fR, \fBembedded\fR); treat it as engine\-owned state.
.SS "Node accessors"
.CS
::tkurender::nodeType   $id
::tkurender::nodeOpt    $id key            ;# widget option value
::tkurender::setOpt     $id key value
::tkurender::nodeName   $id                ;# handle name ("" if unnamed)
::tkurender::setName    $id name
::tkurender::nodeGeom   $id ?key?          ;# grid/pack geometry dict
::tkurender::setGeom    $id key value
::tkurender::nodeLayout $id                ;# child layout: grid|pack|place
::tkurender::setLayout  $id mode
::tkurender::setStretch $id row|col idx weight
.CE
.SS Catalogue
.CS
::tkurender::isContainer $type             ;# 1 if it may hold children
::tkurender::optspecOf   $type             ;# option-editing spec
::tkurender::labelOf     $type             ;# palette label
::tkurender::pkgFor      $type             ;# required package, or ""
::tkurender::pkgAvail    $type             ;# 1 if that package can load
.CE
.PP
Leaf types whose widget lives in another package (e.g. \fBtkunumentry\fR, \fBtablelist\fR) report it via \fBpkgFor\fR; the renderer substitutes a labelled placeholder when the package is missing instead of failing.
.SS Render
.CS
::tkurender::renderChildren $::tkurender::D(root) $parentW $pv
.CE
.PP
Builds the live widget tree for the model under \fB$parentW\fR. Afterwards \fBD(wpath,<id>)\fR maps each node id to its widget path. Selection is decoupled: the engine binds \fB<Button\-1>\fR only when \fB::tkurender::selectCmd\fR is set \-\- the designer sets it, the loader leaves it empty, so loaded UIs carry no editor bindings.
.SS Persistence
.CS
set spec [::tkurender::serialize]          ;# a plain Tcl dict (a .tkd file)
::tkurender::deserialize $spec
.CE
.PP
\fBdeserialize\fR is forward\-compatible: a node missing an option that was added to the catalogue later silently receives the current default, so older \fB.tkd\fR files keep loading.
.SS Errors
.PP
Carry \fB{TKUTILS DESIGNER <REASON>}\fR: \fBPARENT\fR (render target missing), \fBSPEC\fR (malformed \fB.tkd\fR on deserialize).
